arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-3f816f099ac5456aa6cb0b57e8230b11/ShipmentTracker/` using:

```
dotnet new blazor -n ShipmentTracker -int Auto -au Individual -f net10.0 --no-https
```

This gives us:
- **ShipmentTracker** (server project) - has `Components/`, `Data/`, `Program.cs`
- **ShipmentTracker.Client** (WASM project) - has `Pages/` with Counter.razor and Auth.razor

The template uses **InteractiveAuto** render mode (Server for fast first load, WASM after) with **Individual accounts** auth (Identity with SQLite).

## Requirements
1. Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Every page involves interactive controls
4. Staff and customers authenticate with individual accounts
5. Role-based access: "Dispatcher" role for staff, "Customer" role for customers

## What to build

### 1. Shared Shipment Model
Create `/tmp/sv-3f816f099ac5456aa6cb0b57e8230b11/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

### 2. Server-side Data Entity
Create `/tmp/sv-3f816f099ac5456aa6cb0b57e8230b11/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:

```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [Required, MaxLength(20)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public int Status { get; set; } // Maps to ShipmentStatus enum

    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }

    [Required, MaxLength(256)]
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(500)]
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

### 3. Update ApplicationDbContext
Edit `/tmp/sv-3f816f099ac5456aa6cb0b57e8230b11/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();

    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder builder)
    {
        base.OnModelCreating(builder);

        builder.Entity<Shipment>(e =>
        {
            e.HasIndex(s => s.TrackingNumber).IsUnique();
            e.HasIndex(s => s.CustomerEmail);
        });
    }
}
